id: pm-65srr0
title: "GH-1514: injected extension SDK client loses invocation author precedence"
description: "Report on published 2026.10.19: ctx.sdk.client writes use a synthetic pm-extension actor instead of PM_AUTHOR or author_default. Explicit author works. Preserve the canonical invocation author chain across injected package clients and keep extension provenance separate. Intake is reported evidence; reproduction and implementation are pending. https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1514"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T18:04:41.544Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T09:31:56.691Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T09:09:05.594Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T09:09:05.594Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce injected-client attribution against core writes; verify environment/default/explicit precedence and scoped restoration; preserve extension provenance and history integrity.
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Removed synthetic pm-extension attribution from host-bound SDK construction, threaded native options.author into the invocation scope, kept host author out of package flag validation, and resolved workspace mutation author provenance through the shared resolver."
expected_result: "Extension SDK item writes follow per-call override, invocation, PM_AUTHOR and workspace default precedence; audited settings retain the outer invocation identity without leaking per-call overrides."
actual_result: "Real CLI/native extension histories and audited settings pass all precedence, provenance and scope-restoration scenarios. Verification: all four source-identical CI-style coverage shards admitted successfully, then strict Vitest merge and exact covered/total gate pass. 835 test files pass, one configured file skip; 10,829 tests pass and 3 skip. Exact source counts: lines 66,222/66,222; statements 69,828/69,828; functions 14,388/14,388; branches 53,664/53,664. Both linked PM commands pass (author 2 tests, list/accounting/dogfood 170). Four TypeScript configurations pass; real package-first workflow passes; mutation gate has 345 killed plus 7 classified equivalents and zero failures. Graph composition passes the unchanged 1233 prose-gap ceiling; record integrity passes. First-head hosted coverage and all six cold transport budgets pass. Full local static timing failure and launcher lease-wait failures remain recorded separately; no budgets, graph bounds, coverage thresholds or exclusions were weakened. Final exact-head hosted static/smoke/security/analyzer checks and fresh reviews remain required on PR #1517 before merge. CodeRabbit first-head full review has no actionable findings; Sourcery, Greptile and Cubic are unavailable under their recorded free-service limits, not approvals. New source remains Unreleased for the next eligible daily publication."
